              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to hum, then the Marathi for to practise music."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अभिनय",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अभिनय — abhinay — \"acting\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "त्या अभिनेत्रीचा अभिनय सगळ्यांना आवडला. tyā abhinetrīcā abhinay sagḷyānnā āvaḍlā. Everyone liked that actress's acting."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अभिनय (abhinay) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit abhinaya, \"expressing a feeling on stage, acting\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
